# Project Context

Multi-tenant SaaS for restaurant staff scheduling (Node.js + Express
backend, Next.js frontend, PostgreSQL + Prisma, HiGHS for scheduling —
no Python anywhere in this repo).

Core workflow: Manager creates a Shift Requirement (per branch,
weekday/weekend day/night staffing counts) → gets a shareable public
link → workers open it with NO account, submit name + employeeId +
availability → manager generates a schedule (HiGHS MIP solver) →
reviews/confirms → workers revisit the SAME link to check their
assigned shifts.

Current scope: single-tenant MVP behavior is fine functionally, but
the Organization/multi-tenant data model must always be respected —
every query filters by the current organizationId.

Full spec: see FINAL-BUILD-PLAN.md at the repo root. Read it before
starting any task that isn't covered by an already-completed prompt.

Do not introduce Python, a separate scheduler microservice, or
worker-account/auth concepts — these were deliberately removed.
